      <div class="center">
        <div class="eyebrow">What You'll Walk Through</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Grace received, before grace given.</h2>
        <p class="lead narrow">The book refuses to start with your wounds. It starts with God — his holy love, the debt none of us can pay, and the cross — and only then turns to receiving forgiveness, forgiving yourself, and forgiving others. You cannot give what you have not received.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="journey-grid">
        <div class="part-card">
          <div class="part-num">Part One</div>
          <h3>The God Who Forgives</h3>
          <p>It begins with God, not your wounds — his holy love, and the debt none of us could ever pay.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="part-card">
          <div class="part-num">Part Two</div>
          <h3>How God Forgives — the Cross</h3>
          <p>Blood and mercy. The great exchange. The wrath borne on your behalf, and the robe placed on your shoulders.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="part-card">
          <div class="part-num">Part Three</div>
          <h3>The Story Through Scripture</h3>
          <p>From Eden to the cross — a people forgiven beyond measure, and a God who cries, "How can I give you up?"</p>
        </div>
        <div class="part-card">
          <div class="part-num">Part Four</div>
          <h3>Receiving Forgiveness</h3>
          <p>The God who forgets to count. Peter's redemption. Freedom from the jail of self-condemnation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="part-card">
          <div class="part-num">Part Five</div>
          <h3>Extending Forgiveness</h3>
          <p>The cost of keeping score — and the hardest forgivings: betrayal, abuse, injustice. Forgiveness, reconciliation, and safety, honestly untangled.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="part-card">
          <div class="part-num">Part Six</div>
          <h3>The Invitation &amp; the Forgiven Life</h3>
          <p>Come and be forgiven — then live it daily. It closes where it must: love God, love people.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
